{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ReSEACT3DChem",
    "description": "ReSEACT 3-D transport on a NATIVE slice of the GEOS-FP 4x5 grid, driven by real GEOS-FP meteorology. NO REGRIDDING: the local grid IS the native grid, so the whole conservative-overlap chain collapses to an index shift. The slice is (LON0, LAT0) + (NLON, NLAT, NLEV): local lon cell i is native LON0+i and local lat point j is native LAT0+j. The defaults 14/29 x 7x7x72 are lon centres -110..-80, lat points 26..50 (the central US); LON0=11 with NLON=13 widens it to -125..-65, the full CONUS span, at the same 4x5 resolution.\n\nTransport is the monotone flux-form PPM stack imported BY REFERENCE from EarthSciDiscretizations: regional open-wall inflow BCs on lon/lat, and the HYBRID sigma-pressure massform vertical (dp = dA[k] + dB[k]*PS(i,j,t)) on lev. The horizontal and vertical rule stack is byte-identical to the verified prototypes/transport_3d/transport_3d.esm; only the FORCING differs — the analytic test winds and constant PS are replaced by GEOS-FP U/V/OMEGA/PS, each supplied by an EarthSciIO discrete_provider returning the TWO records bracketing the solver time and blended continuously in time (records_per_sample=2 + w_time, the era5 pattern).\n\nGEOS-FP's collections are not co-phased, so three independent weights are used: w_I3 (PS, 3-hourly instantaneous at 00:00Z), w_A3 (U/V/OMEGA, 3-hourly means at 01:30Z) and w_A1 (PBLH, hourly means at 00:30Z).\n\nFace fluxes follow the metric the ESD divergence stencils imply on the unit sphere: Mx = dp_face*U_face/a and My = dp_face*V_face/a (Pa/s, matching m in Pa), with the A-grid GEOS-FP winds averaged to faces. Mz is NOT taken from GEOS-FP's OMEGA. It is DIAGNOSED from continuity, the standard offline-CTM construction: integrating dm_k/dt = -(divh_fix_k + Mz[k+1] - Mz[k]) upward from a rigid ground with the requirement that m reproduce the hydrostatic thickness gives Mz[ke] = -sum_{k<ke}(dB[k]*dPSdt + divh_fix[k]), +ve UPWARD at each cell's LOWER edge. Mz[1] = 0 falls out as the empty sum and Mz[NLEV+1] = 0 because sum_k dB[k] = 1 and the pressure fixer makes sum_k divh_fix[k] = -dPSdt exactly -- so the diagnosed field satisfies the no-flux walls the massform stencils already assume, rather than merely being clipped by them. Using OMEGA directly instead is what made m drift from dp; see caveat (4).\n\nCHEMISTRY + PHOTOLYSIS. The SuperFast gas-phase mechanism (EarthSciModels components/gaschem/superfast.esm) is lifted onto the slice by operator_compose with pointwise lifting, and its six photolysis rates come from the Fast-JX component (components/gaschem/fastjx/fastjx_interp_troposphere.esm) rather than being fixed numbers.\n\nWHICH Fast-JX, and why. The fastjx/ directory holds two variants. fastjx.esm computes the solar position itself from (lat, lon, t_utc) and then scales each of its 18 actinic-flux bands as max(0, cos_sza * const_i) — no pressure dependence at all. fastjx_interp_troposphere.esm instead takes cos_sza as an INPUT and interpolates the flux bilinearly on a real (cos_sza, P) table. The second is mounted here for two independent reasons. (a) Physics: the bilinear table gives the flux genuine vertical structure through P, which the linear-in-cos_sza form cannot. (b) Tractability: fastjx.esm's solar block runs datetime.day_of_year / datetime.hour / minute / second on its t_utc, and EarthSciAST evaluates the datetime.* family as OPAQUE host calls (Dates.unix2datetime). Those cannot take the solver time t, and under Reactant they cannot take even a literal — the tree-walk evaluator lowers every leaf as convert(T, ...), and T is a TracedRNumber, so the trace dies inside the callee. Taking cos_sza as an input moves the solar geometry to this side, where it is pure arithmetic.\n\nSo Transport3D grows a small solar chain: doy0 / hour0 / min0 / sec0 decompose the CALENDAR once at the model's t=0 epoch (2016-01-01T00:00:00Z) as plain literals, and gamma_s -> decl_s -> eqtime_s -> tstmin_s -> cos_sza_c advance it with the NOAA Spencer-Fourier formulas copied term for term from fastjx.esm, with the elapsed time entering as t/86400 (fractional year) and t/60 (true solar time). The sun therefore MOVES with the solve instead of being frozen at the window start, and the result agrees bit for bit with the upstream form at whole hours past the epoch (between them it is smoother — upstream truncates `hour` to an integer).\n\nFast-JX has no ODEs, so it is NOT operator_composed; it is lifted purely by SHAPE. Four param_to_var edges hand it grid-shaped inputs — cos_sza_c, Tc and Pc (the same GEOS-FP temperature and hybrid mid-layer pressure SuperFast reads), plus the scalar water H2Oc — and promote_downstream_shapes then carries [lon,lat,lev] through the whole flux -> cross-section -> j-rate chain. Six more edges map j_H2O2 / j_H2COa / j_H2COb / j_CH3OOH / j_NO2 / j_o32OH onto SuperFast's jH2O2 / jH2COa / jH2COb / jCH3OOH / jNO2 / jO32OH (the wiring of the EarthSciModels coupling library couplings/fastjx_superfast.esm, spelled out inline — see the first of those edges for why). The splitter's stencil_vs_pointwise rule puts the entire photolysis chain in the POINTWISE half, alongside the chemistry it drives.\n\nCAVEATS. (1) PS is read in hPa and scaled by 100 — the loader declares Pa but EarthSciIO returns raw file values. (2) The lev no-flux BC is baked into the stencils (they never read Mz[1] or Mz[NLEV+1]), so the 7-level slab is CLOSED at its ~906 hPa top even though real air flows through it — a truncated-column artifact, negligible over the 1 s first-light window but not for long runs. (3) The two end lat rows are half-width (lat_edge clamps them) while native lat cells are a full 4 deg. (4) PRESSURE FIXER, and the mass source it implies. GEOS-FP's A3 winds are 3-hourly MEANS while its I3 surface pressure is INSTANTANEOUS, so the two disagree: the column-integrated horizontal mass divergence divh_col does not equal -dPSdt, and the discrete identity d(dp)/dt + div(M) = 0 fails (Jockel et al. 2001). Left alone, m wandered away from dp = dA[k] + dB[k]*PS at ~3e-6 1/s and the long runs died of it. The fixer is COLUMN-LOCAL: divh_fix = divh + (-dPSdt - divh_col)*dp/dp_col spreads the column imbalance over the levels by dp weight, Mz is diagnosed from divh_fix, and -- this is the part that has to match -- the CONTINUITY equation reads the same divh_fix. Pairing a divh_fix-derived Mz with the raw divergence leaves the correction uncancelled and reproduces the drift almost exactly; that was a real bug, caught by tools/continuity_residual.jl, whose signature is a residual that is CONSTANT down each column in dp-relative terms. With both sides consistent, dm_k/dt = dB[k]*dPSdt to roundoff -- measured 1.3e-17 1/s rms (max 3.5e-16) on the RHS itself over a 7x7x72 slice, and integrating for 30 simulated minutes leaves max|m - dp|/dp at 2.6e-13, growing SUBLINEARLY across the six macro steps (1.05, 1.77, 1.98, 2.21, 2.54, 2.61 e-13), which is bounded accumulation roundoff rather than a residual bias. Note what this does and does not buy. The column budget is OVER-DETERMINED -- sum_k dm_k/dt is pinned to -divh_col by the no-flux top and bottom walls whatever Mz does, while the target sums to dPSdt -- so making m track dp REQUIRES a mass source equal to that imbalance (~4e-6 1/s here, ~1.3% of column mass per hour). This form ABSORBS it rather than eliminating it. Eliminating it means adjusting Mx and My so divh_col == -dPSdt, a 2-D Poisson solve for a velocity potential, which is not a column-local operation and is not what this is. Composition is untouched either way: the species stay in CWC mixing-ratio form with the RAW div(M), which is exactly the mixing-ratio equation implied by carrying the source at the local mixing ratio, so the correction cancels out of dq/dt identically. CWC is verified, not asserted: tools/cwc_gate.jl synthesises a gate copy of this model and finds max|q-1| == 0 EXACTLY in both the mixing-ratio form the species use and the mass form mqg/mg, with tracer mass bitwise equal to air mass throughout, and each of the three axes' tracer-vs-continuity divergence difference exactly 0.0 at every cell -- including through the diagnosed Mz. (The composite three-axis sum shows ~1e-17, which the per-axis states prove is the association order of two sums of bitwise-identical addends in the emitted code, not the operator.) (5) FastJX.H2O is the REAL 3-D field (Transport3D.Qc, from GEOS-FP I3 specific humidity QV). It started life as a single tropospheric scalar and that turned out to be fatal, not cosmetic: the O(1D)+H2O -> 2OH branching depends on the H2O MIXING RATIO alone, so a constant 1.84% overstates the OH yield ~3,320x above 12 km and drove a HOx runaway that killed the solver 20 simulated minutes into a dawn run at NLEV=72. NOTE the remaining inconsistency: SuperFast's own H2O is still a constant 1.839e7 ppb reservoir, so the mechanism and the photolysis now disagree about humidity aloft. Coupling Transport3D.Qc -> SuperFast.H2O would close that, but it changes the MECHANISM's water, not just a photolysis input. (6) Fast-JX here is the TROPOSPHERIC table. Its (cos_sza, P) flux lookup already has a CLIMATOLOGICAL clear-sky overhead-ozone column baked in — that is exactly what makes it usable at the surface, and why its j_O31D at overhead sun (3.4e-5 1/s, the textbook value) is ~206x smaller than the sibling fastjx.esm's unattenuated max(0, cos_sza*const_i) form (6.9e-3 1/s, a top-of-atmosphere number). What is NOT modelled is any VARIATION about that climatology: no prognostic O3 column, no cloud, no aerosol, no surface albedo. The P axis spans 1000..100000 Pa, so the surface layer at ~101325 Pa clamps to the last column (a 1.3% extrapolation declined); every level above is interpolated. (7) The upstream fastjx_interp_troposphere.esm carried a trivial `NO2` state with D(NO2) = -j_NO2*NO2 purely as an \"ODE skeleton\" for its example plots. That state is incompatible with mounting the component on a grid — once cos_sza/T/P arrive per cell every observed is promoted to [lon,lat,lev], leaving a SCALAR state with an array-valued RHS — so it was removed upstream, making the component stateless like its sibling fastjx.esm. Its three inline tests assert only J-rates and F_i at t=0 and are unaffected. (8) The tables' ABSOLUTE calibration is inherited, not audited here: at overhead sun they give j_NO2 = 2.1e-3 1/s, where the commonly cited clear-sky noon value is nearer 8e-3 1/s (the sibling fastjx.esm gives 3.9e-3). j_O31D, by contrast, lands on the textbook value. Both components come from the same GasChem.jl migration, so a low j_NO2 normalisation is an UPSTREAM question, not an artifact of this model's wiring — flagged because photolysis of NO2 sets the NOx-O3 photostationary state and therefore most of the O3 response seen here.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:latlon3d",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "op:D",
      "axes:lon,lat,lev",
      "scheme:flux_form",
      "property:free_stream",
      "bc:inflow"
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLON": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 7,
      "description": "Zonal cell count of the native GEOS-FP 4x5 slice (1..57: east halo native LON0+NLON+1 <= 72). Bound at load; folds the transport template dims."
    },
    "NLAT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 7,
      "description": "Meridional cell count of the slice (1..17: top lat point native LAT0+NLAT <= 46). Drives the lat-edge clamp min(gje,NLAT)."
    },
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 72,
      "description": "Vertical level count (1..72: hybrid-coef table length). Drives the lev-edge clamp min(gke,NLEV); a value <72 is a truncated column (dA/dB sliced by the host)."
    },
    "LON0": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 14,
      "description": "Zonal origin of the native GEOS-FP 4x5 slice: local lon cell i is native cell LON0+i, so LON0=14 puts i=1 at native 15 (centre -110) and LON0=11 puts it at native 12 (centre -125, the west edge of CONUS). Bound at load. Must satisfy LON0 >= 1 (the west halo reads native LON0) and LON0+NLON+1 <= 72 (the east halo). The `Transport3D.lon0_deg` PARAMETER carries the same origin in degrees and must be overridden to match: lon0_deg = -182.5 + 5*LON0."
    },
    "LAT0": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 29,
      "description": "Meridional origin of the slice: local lat point j is native point LAT0+j, so LAT0=29 puts j=1 at native 30 (26 degN). Bound at load. Must satisfy LAT0 >= 1 (the south flank reads native LAT0) and LAT0+NLAT <= 46. The `Transport3D.lat0_deg` PARAMETER carries the same origin in degrees and must be overridden to match: lat0_deg = -90 + 4*LAT0."
    },
    "NEI_NX": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 459,
      "description": "Column count of the NEI2016 12US1 source grid (IOAPI NCOLS). Fixed by the data product, not by the run. Ties the source ring builder's GX, the NSRC index-set size, and the (row, col) flattening of the native array to one number."
    },
    "NEI_NY": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 299,
      "description": "Row count of the NEI2016 12US1 source grid (IOAPI NROWS)."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "GEOSFP": {
      "ref": "../EarthSciModels/components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm"
    },
    "FastJX": {
      "ref": "../EarthSciModels/components/gaschem/fastjx/fastjx_interp_troposphere.esm"
    },
    "Transport3D": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lon_open_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": "NLON",
            "NLAT": "NLAT",
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lat_open_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": "NLON",
            "NLAT": "NLAT",
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lon_mono_inflow_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": "NLON",
            "NLAT": "NLAT",
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lat_mono_inflow_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": "NLON",
            "NLAT": "NLAT",
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lev_mono_hybrid_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": "NLON",
            "NLAT": "NLAT",
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../EarthSciDiscretizations/grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lev_massform_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": "NLON",
            "NLAT": "NLAT",
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "m": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Air mass per cell (a pressure thickness). Strictly positive."
        },
        "lon0_deg": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": -112.5,
          "description": "West EDGE of the slice, in degrees. GEOS-FP 4x5 lon cell edges are -182.5+5*(i-1), so this MUST be kept equal to -182.5 + 5*LON0 -- it is the degree-space twin of the LON0 metaparameter and nothing in the model derives one from the other (a parameter default cannot be an expression over a metaparameter). The default -112.5 is the edge of native cell i=15, matching LON0=14. `native_slice` in split_common.jl derives both from one origin; set them by hand and they can disagree silently, which shifts the SOLAR ZENITH ANGLE off the transported air without shifting the meteorology."
        },
        "lat0_deg": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 26.0,
          "description": "Southern-most lat POINT of the slice, in degrees. GEOS-FP 4x5 lat points are -90+4*(j-1), so this MUST be kept equal to -90 + 4*LAT0 -- the degree-space twin of the LAT0 metaparameter (see lon0_deg for why it is not derived). The default 26.0 is native j=30, matching LAT0=29."
        },
        "dlon_deg": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "deg",
          "expression": 5.0,
          "description": "GEOS-FP 4x5 native zonal spacing. Open west/east walls (regional, not periodic)."
        },
        "dlat_deg": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "deg",
          "expression": 4.0,
          "description": "GEOS-FP 4x5 native meridional spacing. Open south/north walls (regional, not polar)."
        },
        "phie": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "deg",
          "shape": [
            "lat_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Latitude cell EDGES from the grid's lat_edge template; the half-polar caps fall out of the clamp at +/-90.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "lat_edge",
            "bindings": {}
          }
        },
        "coslat_e": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lat_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "cos of the latitude edges. Zero-length face at each pole. Never read at faces 1 or NLAT+1 -- the pole terms are structurally omitted.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "coslat_edge",
            "bindings": {
              "phie": "phie"
            }
          }
        },
        "dS_lat": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lat"
          ],
          "description": "Exact spherical cell-area weight sin(phie[j+1]) - sin(phie[j]).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "latcell_area",
            "bindings": {
              "phie": "phie"
            }
          }
        },
        "dphi_lat": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "rad",
          "shape": [
            "lat"
          ],
          "description": "Meridional cell extent; HALF-width at the two polar caps.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "latcell_dphi",
            "bindings": {
              "phie": "phie"
            }
          }
        },
        "Mx": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "Pa/s",
          "shape": [
            "lon_nodes",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Zonal face-normal AIR-MASS flux (Pa/s) at each lon face: Mx = dp_face * U_face / a, the metric the ESD divergence stencil implies on the unit sphere (cell area dlon_rad*dS_lat, zonal face length dphi_lat). dp_face and U_face are 2-point averages of the two native cells flanking the face (LON0-1+ie, LON0+ie) — exact, because each local lon cell has the same footprint as native cell LON0+i and the local edges sit on native cell midpoints. Replaces the Stage-B analytic wind. The west/east wall faces (ie=1, ie=NLON+1) are GENUINE faces on an open domain, and their halo cells (native LON0 and LON0+NLON+1) exist in the native array — no extrapolation needed.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "gie",
              "gj",
              "gk"
            ],
            "args": [
              "F_PS",
              "F_U",
              "dA",
              "dB"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "gie": {
                "from": "lon_nodes"
              },
              "gj": {
                "from": "lat"
              },
              "gk": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        0.5,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "index",
                                  "args": [
                                    "dA",
                                    "gk"
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "index",
                                      "args": [
                                        "dB",
                                        "gk"
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "op": "*",
                                      "args": [
                                        100.0,
                                        {
                                          "op": "+",
                                          "args": [
                                            {
                                              "op": "*",
                                              "args": [
                                                {
                                                  "op": "-",
                                                  "args": [
                                                    1.0,
                                                    "w_I3"
                                                  ]
                                                },
                                                {
                                                  "op": "index",
                                                  "args": [
                                                    "F_PS",
                                                    1,
                                                    {
                                                      "op": "+",
                                                      "args": [
                                                        "LAT0",
                                                        "gj"
                                                      ]
                                                    },
                                                    {
                                                      "op": "+",
                                                      "args": [
                                                        {
                                                          "op": "-",
                                                          "args": [
                                                            "LON0",
                                                            1
                                                          ]
                                                        },
                                                        "gie"
                                                      ]
                                                    }
                                                  ]
                                                }
                                              ]
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "op": "*",
                                              "args": [
                                                "w_I3",
                                                {
                                                  "op": "index",
                                                  "args": [
                                                    "F_PS",
                                                    2,
                                                    {
                                                      "op": "+",
                                                      "args": [
                                                        "LAT0",
                                                        "gj"
                                                      ]
                                                    },
                                                    {
                                                      "op": "+",
                                                      "args": [
                                                        {
                                                          "op": "-",
                                                          "args": [
                                                            "LON0",
                                                            1
                                                          ]
                                                        },
                                                        "gie"
                                                      ]
                                                    }
                                                  ]
                                                }
                                              ]
                                            }
                                          ]
                                        }
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "index",
                                  "args": [
                                    "dA",
                                    "gk"
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "index",
                                      "args": [
                                        "dB",
                                        "gk"
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "op": "*",
                                      "args": [
                                        100.0,
                                        {
                                          "op": "+",
                                          "args": [
                                            {
                                              "op": "*",
                                              "args": [
                                                {
                                                  "op": "-",
                                                  "args": [
                                                    1.0,
                                                    "w_I3"
                                                  ]
                                                },
                                                {
                                                  "op": "index",
                                                  "args": [
                                                    "F_PS",
                                                    1,
                                                    {
                                                      "op": "+",
                                                      "args": [
                                                        "LAT0",
                                                        "gj"
                                                      ]
                                                    },
                                                    {
                                                      "op": "+",
                                                      "args": [
                                                        "LON0",
                                                        "gie"
                                                      ]
                                                    }
                                                  ]
                                                }
                                              ]
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "op": "*",
                                              "args": [
                                                "w_I3",
                                                {
                                                  "op": "index",
                                                  "args": [
                                                    "F_PS",
                                                    2,
                                                    {
                                                      "op": "+",
                                                      "args": [
                                                        "LAT0",
                                                        "gj"
                                                      ]
                                                    },
                                                    {
                                                      "op": "+",
                                                      "args": [
                                                        "LON0",
                                                        "gie"
                                                      ]
                                                    }
                                                  ]
                                                }
                                              ]
                                            }
                                          ]
                                        }
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        0.5,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "-",
                                      "args": [
                                        1.0,
                                        "w_A3"
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "op": "index",
                                      "args": [
                                        "F_U",
                                        1,
                                        "gk",
                                        {
                                          "op": "+",
                                          "args": [
